.TH KERN 1 "2025-11-03" "kern v1.2.0" "System Monitoring Tool"
.SH NAME
kern \- real-time system monitoring tool with TUI and REST API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kern
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B kern
\fB\-a\fR | \fB\-\-all\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-c\fR | \fB\-\-cpu\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-d\fR | \fB\-\-disk\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-m\fR | \fB\-\-mem\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-n\fR | \fB\-\-net\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-g\fR | \fB\-\-gpu\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-\-ai\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-\-mining\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-r\fR [\fIPORT\fR] | \fB\-\-remote\fR [\fIPORT\fR]
.br
.B kern
\fB\-\-api\fR \fIURL\fR
.br
.B kern
\fB\-\-ssh\fR \fIHOST\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kern
is a comprehensive system monitoring tool that provides real-time information about system resources including disk usage, CPU performance, memory utilization, network statistics, GPU metrics, AI training processes, and cryptocurrency mining activity.

The tool features a professional Terminal User Interface (TUI) with double buffering to eliminate screen flickering, support for multiple languages with automatic download capability, and multi-protocol remote monitoring via HTTP, HTTPS, and SSH.

.B kern
automatically starts a background API server on port 28126 during installation, providing immediate access to monitoring data via REST API without any manual configuration.

.B kern
remembers your last used monitoring modules and will automatically show them when run without arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show all system information. This is the default behavior on first run.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cpu
Show CPU information only, including model, cores, threads, usage percentage, frequency, and load averages.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-disk
Show disk information only, including filesystem type, size, usage, and mount points.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mem
Show memory information only, including RAM and swap usage with visual graphs.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-net
Show network information only, including interface status, IP/MAC addresses, and traffic statistics.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-gpu
Show GPU information only. Requires NVIDIA drivers (nvidia-smi) or AMD ROCm (rocm-smi).
.TP
.B \-\-ai
Show AI training information only, including framework detection, VRAM usage, and training metrics.
.TP
.B \-\-mining
Show cryptocurrency mining information only, including algorithm, hashrate, and efficiency metrics.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information and application logo.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show comprehensive help message.
.TP
.BI \-\-refresh= SECONDS
Set refresh interval in seconds. Default is 2 seconds. Minimum is 1 second.
.TP
.BI \-l " LANG" "\fR, " \-\-lang " LANG"
Set interface language. Language pack must be downloaded first using \fB\-\-download-lang\fR. Use \fB\-\-list-languages\fR to see all supported codes.
.TP
.BI \-r " [PORT]" "\fR, " \-\-remote " [PORT]"
Start remote API server on specified port. Default port is 28126 if not specified.
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Show detailed CPU core information including individual core usage percentages.
.TP
.BI \-\-api " URL"
Monitor remote server via HTTP/HTTPS API. URL should be in format http://host:port or https://host:port.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh " HOST"
Monitor remote server via SSH. Format should be user@hostname.
.TP
.BI \-\-download-lang " CODE"
Download language pack for specified language code. The language will be available for use after download.
.TP
.B \-\-list-languages
List all supported language codes with their full names.
.TP
.B \-\-logo
Show application logo during monitoring display.
.TP
.B \-\-start-service
Start the kern daemon service.
.TP
.B \-\-stop-service
Stop the kern daemon service.
.TP
.B \-\-restart-service
Restart the kern daemon service.
.TP
.B \-\-service-status
Show daemon service status information.
.TP
.B \-\-enable-service
Enable auto-start of kern daemon on system boot.
.TP
.B \-\-disable-service
Disable auto-start of kern daemon.
.TP
.B \-\-ensure-running
Ensure daemon is running (automatically starts if not running).
.SH AUTOMATIC BACKGROUND API
.B kern
automatically starts a background API server on port 28126 during installation. This server provides REST API access to all monitoring data without requiring manual intervention.

The API server starts automatically on system boot if auto-start is enabled (default behavior).

.SH TUI CONTROLS
When running in interactive TUI mode, the following controls are available:
.TP
.B q ", " Q ", " ESC
Quit the application gracefully.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Quit the application (same as q).
.TP
.B Terminal Resize
Interface automatically adapts to terminal size changes and redraws appropriately.
.SH SMART MODULE PREFERENCES
.B kern
automatically remembers which modules you used last and will show them when you run the program without any arguments.

Example:
.IP
$ kern --gpu --ai
.br
# kern remembers GPU and AI modules
.br
$ kern
.br
# Shows only GPU and AI information (your last used modules)
.br
$ kern --all
.br
# Resets to show all modules
.SH REMOTE MONITORING
.B kern
supports multiple remote monitoring protocols for distributed system monitoring:
.SS HTTP/HTTPS API
Access kern API servers running on remote machines:
.IP
.B Remote machine:
kern -r 28126
.br
.B Local machine:
kern --api http://remote-ip:28126
.SS SSH Monitoring
Execute kern directly on remote machines via SSH:
.IP
kern --ssh user@remote-host
.br
kern --ssh user@remote-host --api http://localhost:28126
.SS Network Access
.IP \(bu 3
Local Network: Access within same network segment
.IP \(bu 3
Global Internet: Access via public IP with port forwarding
.IP \(bu 3
VPN Networks: Access through corporate or private VPNs
.IP \(bu 3
Cloud Instances: Monitor AWS, GCP, Azure VMs
.SH API ENDPOINTS
When running in server mode (\fB-r\fR), kern provides these REST API endpoints:
.TP
.B GET /api/cpu
Returns JSON with CPU information, usage, and load averages.
.TP
.B GET /api/mem
Returns JSON with memory and swap usage information.
.TP
.B GET /api/disk
Returns JSON with disk usage and filesystem information.
.TP
.B GET /api/net
Returns JSON with network interfaces and traffic statistics.
.TP
.B GET /api/gpu
Returns JSON with GPU information, temperature, and utilization.
.TP
.B GET /api/ai
Returns JSON with AI training processes and VRAM usage.
.TP
.B GET /api/mining
Returns JSON with mining activity and efficiency metrics.
.TP
.B GET /api/system
Returns JSON with system information and kern version.
.TP
.B GET /health
Returns health status check.
.TP
.B GET /
Returns API information and available endpoints.
.SH GPU MONITORING
GPU monitoring requires specific drivers and utilities:
.TP
.B NVIDIA GPUs
Requires nvidia-smi utility (included with NVIDIA drivers).
Install with: sudo apt install nvidia-driver-535 nvidia-utils-535
.TP
.B AMD GPUs
Requires rocm-smi utility (included with ROCm).
Install with: sudo apt install rocm-smi-lib
.PP
GPU monitoring provides:
.IP \(bu 3
Temperature and utilization metrics
.IP \(bu 3
Memory usage (VRAM) and capacity
.IP \(bu 3
Power consumption and limits
.IP \(bu 3
Core and memory clock speeds
.IP \(bu 3
Fan speed and performance state
.SH AI TRAINING MONITORING
AI training detection monitors for these frameworks:
.IP \(bu 3
TensorFlow and Keras
.IP \(bu 3
PyTorch and TorchVision
.IP \(bu 3
HuggingFace Transformers
.IP \(bu 3
Jupyter notebooks
.IP \(bu 3
Custom training scripts
.PP
AI metrics include:
.IP \(bu 3
Active training processes count
.IP \(bu 3
VRAM usage and allocation
.IP \(bu 3
Model name and batch size
.IP \(bu 3
Training throughput (samples/sec)
.IP \(bu 3
Loss and accuracy metrics
.IP \(bu 3
Epoch progress and training time
.SH MINING MONITORING
Mining detection identifies popular mining software and algorithms:
.TP
.B Supported Algorithms
RandomX (Monero), Ethash (Ethereum), SHA-256 (Bitcoin), KAWPOW (Ravencoin), BeamHash (Beam)
.TP
.B Detected Software
xmrig, cgminer, bfgminer, ethminer, t-rex, lolminer, nbminer, phoenixminer, gminer
.PP
Mining metrics include:
.IP \(bu 3
Hashrate and algorithm detection
.IP \(bu 3
Valid and invalid shares
.IP \(bu 3
GPU temperature and power usage
.IP \(bu 3
Mining efficiency (hash/watt)
.IP \(bu 3
Uptime and pool information
.IP \(bu 3
24-hour revenue estimation
